      "totalDuration": "1 yr 11 mos",
      "description": "I served as the front end technical lead for Bluemix’s CI/CD service, Delivery Pipeline.  The application plays a central role in IBM Cloud's Devops and Continuous Delivery offerings.  The UI is built using a modern technology stack involving, Node, React, Webpack, JQuery, HTML templating engines, and Sass/Less.  We develop using DevOps best practices; so my responsibility included the full spectrum of the software development lifecycle, from design and architecture, to development and test, and through production deployments.\n\nI also led and drove the implementation of BSS support for Continuous Delivery on IBM Bluemix, which integrated our DevOps Services into the Bluemix Service Catalog with support for metrics and usage metering.\n\nLed the UI development of an experimental feature called Composite Pipeline which introduced a new CI/CD visualization and management of multiple applications (both cloud native and on-premises) across multiple environments.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Development Lead - Rational Quality Manager",
      "locationName": "Research Triangle Park, NC",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 8,
        "year": 2007
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 6,
        "year": 2015
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "7 yrs 11 mos",
      "description": "The original developer on a hand picked team to enter a new market segment for the former Rational Brand. Our mission was to build a new product focused on the software testing lifecycle. The team built the product on top of “Jazz”, a new emerging technology platform and by adhering to a new practice, “Open Commercial Software Development”. (https://jazz.net/)\n\n* Following an agile and continuous development process, led globally distributed teams to successfully deliver multiple major releases.\n\n* Core responsibilities include architecting and developing server side Java components on top of a Java EE/OSGI framework.  In addition, I was involved in IBM’s strategic Collaborative Lifecycle Management focusing on integration with other Rational products such as Rational Team Concert and Requirements Management solutions.\n\n* Key development work included an extensible editor framework with transactional based save mechanism, an audit & history framework, resource snapshotting abilities, data migration, formal review/approval of artifacts, and process/governance integration.\n\n* Led the team in an effort to bring a PLE (Product Line Engineering) and configuration management solution across the entire development lifecycle. My focus was to design and develop the underlying capability for the solution, a native, scalable version control system within the Quality Manager application.\n\n* In addition to the primary role of development lead, also held the position of Security Focal point reporting to the organization’s director. Responsibilities included leading the security leads across each product in the organization to implement IBM Software Group initiatives and maintain compliance around the security of our products.",
      "insights": ""
     }
